H1 verdicts are stated per metric at the three tested tiers only and are never extrapolated between capacities. H2 is one four-cell family: each target and each "reaches the target" claim is scoped to that cell's paired cohort, with the baseline's own-cohort mean shown separately. The yaw block is descriptive. The M tier is exp_01's pair re-evaluated under exp_05's protocol; its training predates this experiment (different day, launcher cadence, unrecorded PYTHONHASHSEED) and no tier pair shares a training realization (one seed per arm, unshared data order and reference draws).

