     5	## 1. Question
     6	
     7	Within one acoustic system (xRIR, K-shot RIR prediction) and one backbone family (a panorama ViT with the token count fixed at 256), does the CylindricalViT encoder (CERPA: per-column gauge alignment, elevation-only positional code, circular relative-position bias) reach lower unseen-room acoustic error than the SimpleViT encoder at every encoder parameter budget (experiment 2 of the user's note), and can a smaller cylindrical encoder match a larger baseline one (experiment 3)?
     8	
